.TH DECAF 1 "2026-09-29" "decaf" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
decaf \- suspend the system after a while
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B decaf on
.I DURATION
.br
.B decaf off
.br
.B decaf status
.br
.B decaf
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B decaf
suspends the system after a given number of seconds, even if other programs
try to keep it awake.
It is meant to be scripted: output on stdout is data only, messages go to
stderr, and every outcome has its own exit status.
.PP
A timer is a transient systemd user unit,
.BR app-decaf.service .
While the unit runs, a suspend is scheduled; there is no other state.
Each user has at most one timer, shared by all their sessions.
.PP
.B decaf
is the opposite of
.BR expresso (1),
which keeps the system awake for a while.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI on " DURATION"
Suspend the system in
.I DURATION
seconds.
.I DURATION
is a whole number from 1 to 2147483647, without sign or leading zeros.
Fails if a timer is already on.
.TP
.B off
Cancel the timer. Returns once it is fully cancelled.
.TP
.B status
Print the timer's state; see
.BR "STATUS OUTPUT" .
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH STATUS OUTPUT
.B status
prints
.IB key = value
lines.
When no timer is on, the only line is
.BR state=off .
When a timer is on, all of these keys are printed, in this order:
.TP
.B state
.BR on .
.TP
.B duration
The
.I DURATION
given to
.BR on .
.TP
.B started
When the timer was set, as a Unix timestamp.
.TP
.B until
When the system suspends, as a Unix timestamp.
.TP
.B remaining
Seconds until then.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
state=on
duration=1800
started=1759158600
until=1759160400
remaining=1740
.fi
.RE
.SH TIMING AND SUSPEND
The deadline is wall-clock time:
.B on 1800
means in 30 minutes from now, and time spent suspended counts.
.PP
Sixty seconds before the deadline, a "Suspending soon" notification gives you
the chance to run
.BR "decaf off" .
If the system resumes within that last minute, the notification appears at
once. Timers of 60 seconds or less have no warning.
.PP
If the system was already asleep at the deadline (you suspended it earlier and
resumed later), the timer is skipped: it ends when the system resumes, without
suspending it again.
Suspending and resuming before the deadline keeps the timer.
.PP
At the deadline the system suspends even if other programs hold locks against
it, such as a download or
.BR expresso (1).
Overriding such a blocking lock needs your password (polkit's
.BR suspend-ignore-inhibit );
a prompt appears at the deadline.
If nobody answers it within 25 seconds, the system does not suspend and the
timer ends as failed.
Without blocking locks there is no prompt.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
The timer unit itself sends desktop notifications, whatever started or stopped
it: when the timer is set ("Decaf on"), shortly before the suspend ("Suspending
soon"), when it is skipped or turned off ("Decaf off"), and when it fails
("Decaf failed", with where to look in the journal).
There is none when the system suspends.
The commands send no notifications themselves, and
.B on
and
.B off
print nothing on success.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
For
.BR status :
a timer is on.
.TP
.B 1
No timer is on
.RB ( status ", " off ).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command or option, invalid or missing
.IR DURATION .
.TP
.B 3
A timer is already on
.RB ( on ).
.TP
.B 4
System error: systemd could not be reached, the timer could not be set or
cancelled, or
.B app-decaf.service
exists but was not started by this version of
.BR decaf .
.SH EXAMPLES
Suspend in 45 minutes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
decaf on 2700
.fi
.RE
.PP
Toggle a 30-minute timer, for example from a keybinding:
.PP
.RS
.nf
decaf off 2>/dev/null || decaf on 1800
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check for a timer, and read when it fires:
.PP
.RS
.nf
if decaf status >/dev/null; then
    date \-d "@$(decaf status | sed \-n 's/^until=//p')"
fi
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
None. There is no configuration file; put your preferred durations in a
keybinding, alias or script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR expresso (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd-run (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR notify-send (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/Davi-S/decaf/issues
